                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a6b073df-bcf4-3f7f-990a-8a38b2b42db5",
                        "entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "glosses": [
                            "этногр. отношения между кумовьями"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2f14be4-84aa-415d-903d-cab94f8a46ef",
                                "sense_id": "a6b073df-bcf4-3f7f-990a-8a38b2b42db5",
                                "text": "В Сибири, на севере и в широких степях заволжских, кто живет за полтораста, за двести верст, тот ближний сосед, а родство, свойство и кумовство считается там чуть не до двадцатого колена."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "994b6038-163d-30f4-b90d-c153b142ef5f",
                        "entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг., неодобр. послабления и поблажки по службе в угоду приятельским отношениям или родственным связям"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7134204d-bccc-49a3-b00a-a7411be166a4",
                                "sense_id": "994b6038-163d-30f4-b90d-c153b142ef5f",
                                "text": "В отчетном году было обмануто 12000 человек; всё больничное дело, как и 20 лет назад, построено на воровстве, дрязгах, сплетнях, кумовстве, на грубом шарлатанстве, и больница по-прежнему представляет из себя учреждение безнравственное и в высшей степени вредное для здоровья жителей."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d7b994ee-1ad0-4868-8f06-9d5b39d3cd23",
                        "source_entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "target_lang_word": "cronyism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cronyism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41717d33-fb1b-3710-be5b-2c616224ad84",
                                        "entry_id": "7fb1b855-c1af-35c0-b242-9cc4e0b1f257",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Favouritism to friends without regard for their qualifications; especially (politics), in their appointment to political positions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bbb113f-90a6-46b9-8084-8174c290fff0",
                                                "sense_id": "41717d33-fb1b-3710-be5b-2c616224ad84",
                                                "text": "[T]he present structure of the collective bargaining agreement, combined with nepotism and cronyism and other abuses in employment and referral practices, have perpetuated the effects of the past discrimination, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bec41cb0-7010-437e-9e03-6b6ea3c3a1a7",
                                                "sense_id": "41717d33-fb1b-3710-be5b-2c616224ad84",
                                                "text": "[Robert L.] Hagist began what he called an \"18 month reform program\" that included revised warehouse procedures and measures to prevent the leakages, shortages, cronyisms, and politicking attributed to the managers and clerks of the various stores."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20f17818-78b0-4720-8142-3310ca21e071",
                                                "sense_id": "41717d33-fb1b-3710-be5b-2c616224ad84",
                                                "text": "If we are going to reauthorize the National Endowment, we need to see to it that the Endowment, in its procedures, are open, one. […] That there is a cessation of a long-term practice of cronyisms on the panels so that artists across the Nation have equal access to this."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fcd828b-e80c-4f94-a52c-ed536c3206b5",
                                                "sense_id": "41717d33-fb1b-3710-be5b-2c616224ad84",
                                                "text": "[C]ommunism is predicated upon a central structure of economic command that is singularly entrusted with allocating resources and making economic decisions. Because of this centralized command structure, communist societies fall prey to the forces of cronyism and influence-peddling as commune members without economic power curry favor with commune leaders that control access to resources."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71509182-e7cc-4690-8e19-70548da487ac",
                                                "sense_id": "41717d33-fb1b-3710-be5b-2c616224ad84",
                                                "text": "Patronage, nepotism, cronyism, abuse of power, and criminal activity flourish, sometimes for decades, in numerous town halls, police stations, and special-purpose government agencies in the suburbs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11ad318d-58f4-46d9-9ba7-7a71ba36aa1f",
                                                "sense_id": "41717d33-fb1b-3710-be5b-2c616224ad84",
                                                "text": "Critics accuse her [von der Leyen] of serious missteps over the pandemic, the Gaza war, alleged cronyism, – and of having a high-handed manner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e7f90bc-5122-31d4-a610-6f12fad3f0d2",
                                        "entry_id": "7fb1b855-c1af-35c0-b242-9cc4e0b1f257",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being friends; friendship; also, the ability or inclination to make friends."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30425892-0bbf-46bc-880d-03e307414f39",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7f90bc-5122-31d4-a610-6f12fad3f0d2",
                                                "text": "[T]he preacher […] was reading to them the duty of loving one another as Christians, But only particularly and exclusively were they to love one another \"as Christians,\" that is as confederates and caballers together in a particular interest, distinct from that of the great family of mankind; […] The benefit to themselves from this Free-masonry sectarian cronyism, (for which the uninitiated world is so much obliged to them) was, to be, that […] [t]he spirit of God was to bear witness with their spirits, and to settle the matter of faith with a degree of conviction, that should render reason superfluous and inquiry unnecessary."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21630c82-81f5-429c-8ef8-1a0bdd7f484a",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7f90bc-5122-31d4-a610-6f12fad3f0d2",
                                                "text": "Our friend the Old Crony, we see, for all his connoisseurship and crony-ism, his regard for a certain piquancy of perfection in the French dress and walk, and his wish that his fair countrywomen would \"take steps\" after their fashion, cannot get rid of the preference in which he was brought up for the beauty of the English countenance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0561e1a-84bf-452f-b0ac-8612ab7a416d",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7f90bc-5122-31d4-a610-6f12fad3f0d2",
                                                "text": "She [the minister's wife] is warned against being drawn into excessive attachments, engrossing intimacies, low and gossiping cronyism, all intermeddling with tales and talebearers, with family breaches, with partisanship, and with ecclesiastical jurisdiction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5dd5b02-6fe0-4d3d-8eca-653999ac1936",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7f90bc-5122-31d4-a610-6f12fad3f0d2",
                                                "text": "[H]e [William Jay] observed, that there were two things which caused religious servants to be too generally disliked. The first was their fondness for religious gossiping, or cronyism, which made them regardless of their time, &c."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6047b73-1dc4-4891-8a50-8f9e7c9d6b2d",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7f90bc-5122-31d4-a610-6f12fad3f0d2",
                                                "text": "Pea-green Hayne was one of my most intimate friends; we occupied rooms vis à vis, and made prison life more than endurable by affectionate cronyism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc690bab-1bbc-4077-9e24-f4876ce83e50",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7f90bc-5122-31d4-a610-6f12fad3f0d2",
                                                "text": "And the Englishman and Irishman went off together in a state of thorough cronyism, the former imagining that he had quite taken in his companion, and entertaining no suspicion that it was rather the other way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a7c70747-768e-48b8-a8f1-c0748048b6d3",
                        "source_entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "target_lang_word": "nepotism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nepotism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1cfba0f-2c4e-387d-92e9-ddf36d21d401",
                                        "entry_id": "930f1f97-dfea-3d1d-a8d9-1afba38ba028",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The favoring of relatives (most strictly) or also personal friends (more broadly) because of their relationship rather than because of their abilities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e094eec8-c7f5-469a-a1e3-ead8b9017385",
                                                "sense_id": "a1cfba0f-2c4e-387d-92e9-ddf36d21d401",
                                                "text": "Nepotism can get you very far in the world if you've got the right connections."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "120bc3b3-847c-4ef3-b8f9-a56f779ddc95",
                                                "sense_id": "a1cfba0f-2c4e-387d-92e9-ddf36d21d401",
                                                "text": "Now retailers even demand deslotting or failure fees, a penalty for trial products that fail to meet their sales objectives. The struggle over display space heavily favors the incumbents and encourages what might be called brand nepotism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db72ffa2-7704-447a-a943-add4d2b6c037",
                                                "sense_id": "a1cfba0f-2c4e-387d-92e9-ddf36d21d401",
                                                "text": "Mr Chen - a member of the national politburo as well as the Shanghai boss - is accused of nepotism and corruption on a grand scale: protecting political allies, granting preferment to his family and looting Shanghai's pension fund."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "440509bc-8ec1-4cf4-b0fa-49543725376d",
                        "source_entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "target_lang_word": "favouritism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "favouritism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab161703-84b3-3fb6-a1eb-1fff4dc4ce7f",
                                        "entry_id": "a49f42eb-6413-3661-9ce9-152cb18406fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The unfair favouring of one person or group at the expense of another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbdacb00-dfd4-4ead-b9f6-0363edfb78c8",
                                                "sense_id": "ab161703-84b3-3fb6-a1eb-1fff4dc4ce7f",
                                                "text": "Heidi Alexander has experience of London. As Transport Secretary, she will also be under pressure not to show favouritism to the capital."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4f2213eb-e529-4b25-be22-7ede5efcb091",
                        "source_entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "target_lang_word": "chumocracy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chumocracy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d7e99b9-6063-316d-ae47-72b603a5780f",
                                        "entry_id": "7328e4b6-99b4-3490-a63d-64fa0c586b14",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of oligarchy: government characterised by nepotism and the frequent appointment to public office of friends or those of similar social background to those in power."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "534bd173-2a78-45f6-9961-b1f868dab107",
                                                "sense_id": "5d7e99b9-6063-316d-ae47-72b603a5780f",
                                                "text": "How thrilling it would have been[…] if [Sadiq] Khan had denounced the [Thames garden] bridge in every way: […] as a symbol of the chummery – the chumocracy, even – that so offends the democratic and egalitarian traditions he is proud to represent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aea3b446-9927-42b1-b865-7e0001b573e9",
                                                "sense_id": "5d7e99b9-6063-316d-ae47-72b603a5780f",
                                                "text": "The sums are so vast, the secrecy so shocking, that “chumocracy” doesn’t begin to capture what Britain has become – redolent as we are of banana republics, the Russian oligarchy and failed states."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a766dab8-cb47-4870-aad9-4d71f4bbc046",
                                                "sense_id": "5d7e99b9-6063-316d-ae47-72b603a5780f",
                                                "text": "Mr Hancock secretly appointed her [Gina Coladangelo] to his department as an unpaid adviser on a six-month contract in March last year. It sparked claims of a “chumocracy” when it became public knowledge in November."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e3a2225a-e84a-4a45-81a8-f584327e31d1",
                        "source_entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "target_lang_word": "Vetternwirtschaft",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Vetternwirtschaft",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66362484-3d9c-3c7f-b9e5-615415d87f34",
                                        "entry_id": "89fc2bf8-8662-3793-925f-306395d26143",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "übermäßige Begünstigung von Verwandten, zum Beispiel bei der Verteilung von Geldern, der Vergabe von Aufträgen oder der Besetzung von Positionen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e22b6bab-2cd2-413d-b120-205d59373636",
                                                "sense_id": "66362484-3d9c-3c7f-b9e5-615415d87f34",
                                                "text": "Der neue Präsident sagte der Korruption und der Vetternwirtschaft den Kampf an."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06193e08-e0dd-4d8f-a747-351a82aa4d44",
                                                "sense_id": "66362484-3d9c-3c7f-b9e5-615415d87f34",
                                                "text": "„Sie will um jeden Preis dieses Symbol des Totalitarismus, der Vetternwirtschaft, der Manipulation und der Verfolgung beseitigen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6344214a-04a8-4f54-8935-f4e602e3e229",
                                                "sense_id": "66362484-3d9c-3c7f-b9e5-615415d87f34",
                                                "text": "„Diese Maßnahmen änderten jedoch nichts an höchst ineffektiven Umverteilungsmaßnahmen, entsprechender weiterer Verschuldung und dem von Vetternwirtschaft und einseitiger Bevorzugung der Punjabis gekennzeichneten undemokratischen Politikstil.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56c6e67c-8646-4c92-9ba8-78ec3713b415",
                                                "sense_id": "66362484-3d9c-3c7f-b9e5-615415d87f34",
                                                "text": "„Der Untersuchungsausschuss will nun prüfen, ob Vettern- und Parteibuchwirtschaft den Ausschlag bei der Besetzung der Präsidentenstelle des Oberverwaltungsgerichts gab oder die Kompetenz der Bewerber.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "96a08167-8899-4149-9d7f-eed09f2da758",
                        "source_entry_id": "043d4d8e-1bb3-3ae1-9eb4-48c5dd36fc65",
                        "target_lang_word": "Günstlingswirtschaft",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Günstlingswirtschaft",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6fa1bd5-afbe-30f6-a43d-e01ed1599e0f",
                                        "entry_id": "0fe8d827-c739-30bf-b8d1-1b7a8aac8048",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Verhältnisse, in denen solche Leute bevorzugt werden (zum Beispiel bei der Vergabe von Ämtern), denen man gewogen ist, die man besonders mag, die aber nicht unbedingt Familienangehörige sind"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d8356ec-229a-4ac2-8bb7-f3befcec2af3",
                                                "sense_id": "f6fa1bd5-afbe-30f6-a43d-e01ed1599e0f",
                                                "text": "Manfred Amerell beschuldigte DFB-Präsident Theo Zwanziger öffentlich der Günstlingswirtschaft."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1246ace1-d67b-4dc4-8bce-bc6b858bc564",
                                                "sense_id": "f6fa1bd5-afbe-30f6-a43d-e01ed1599e0f",
                                                "text": "Auf Kosten der Allgemeinheit errichteten die Funktionäre eine völlig intransparente kommunistische Günstlingswirtschaft ohne demokratische Kontrollmöglichkeiten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79105521-7327-41c0-83d3-cc7da1335972",
                                                "sense_id": "f6fa1bd5-afbe-30f6-a43d-e01ed1599e0f",
                                                "text": "In seinen Reden benennt Berlusconi einige Hauptprobleme des Landes: verkommene Schulen und Universitäten, Günstlingswirtschaft, ineffiziente Justiz, Benachteiligung von Frauen im Beruf, Umweltzerstörung, eine bürgerfeindliche Verwaltung und ein byzantinisch-kompliziertes Regierungssystem."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
